Pinta 3.1.2 for Raspberry Pi 5
==============================

This is an unofficial arm64 build of Pinta 3.1.2 for Raspberry Pi OS
Bookworm (Debian 12).  Upstream Pinta 3.1.2 expects GTK 4.10+ and
libadwaita 1.6+, so the source was backported to the GTK 4.8.3 /
libadwaita 1.2.2 stack that ships with Bookworm.

The .NET 8 runtime is bundled under /usr/lib/pinta-3.1.2.  No system-wide
dotnet installation is required, and this package does not depend on the
Microsoft or Debian dotnet packages.  librsvg2-common is a package
dependency because Pinta uses SVG icons.

Installation
------------

    sudo apt install ./pinta-3.1.2_3.1.2+rpi5backport2_arm64.deb

Run:

    pinta-3.1.2 [FILE...]

or use the "Pinta 3.1.2" entry in the application menu.

Coexistence with Pinta 2.1.x
----------------------------

The package installs /usr/bin/pinta-3.1.2 and /usr/lib/pinta-3.1.2.  It
does not touch /usr/local/bin/pinta or /usr/local/lib/pinta, so an
existing Pinta 2.1.x installation remains available as "pinta".

If the old 2.1.x desktop entry is also visible in the application menu,
it can be hidden by adding NoDisplay=true to its .desktop file; the
"pinta" command remains available.

Backport changes
----------------

The upstream 3.1.2 source (commit b3df1e5) was patched for GTK 4.8 /
libadwaita 1.2:

  * Adw.ToolbarView replaced with a vertical Gtk.Box
  * Gtk.FileDialog replaced with Gtk.FileChooserNative
  * Gtk.FontDialogButton replaced with Gtk.FontButton
  * Gtk.UriLauncher replaced with gtk_show_uri()
  * Gtk.Snapshot.AppendScaledTexture replaced with AppendTexture
  * Gdk.MemoryTextureBuilder replaced with GdkPixbuf +
    Gdk.Texture.NewForPixbuf
  * gtk_css_provider_load_from_bytes replaced with
    gtk_css_provider_load_from_data
  * fixed a GSList double-free in GdkPixbuf format enumeration
  * set the application icon and program name so the taskbar icon is
    correct
  * added the application-local icons directory to GTK's icon search
    path so the Adjustments and Effects header icons resolve in the
    self-contained layout
  * switched effects-default-symbolic to currentColor so GTK 4.8 can
    recolor it

The full patch is installed as
/usr/share/doc/pinta-3.1.2/pinta-3.1.2-gtk48-backport.patch.gz.

Known limitations
-----------------

  * The canvas texture is converted from Cairo ARGB32 to a GdkPixbuf in
    managed code, because Debian builds gdk-pixbuf without Cairo support
    (gdk_pixbuf_get_from_surface is unavailable).  Very large canvases
    may redraw more slowly than upstream Pinta on newer GTK.
  * File dialogs use Gtk.FileChooserNative.  Install
    xdg-desktop-portal-gtk for the best desktop integration.
  * The font chooser uses Gtk.FontButton (GTK 4.8).
  * Links are opened with gtk_show_uri().
  * GTK 4.10+ features (for example, scaled-texture filter hints) are
    not available.

Building from source
--------------------

  git clone https://github.com/PintaProject/Pinta.git
  cd Pinta
  git checkout 3.1.2
  patch -p1 < /path/to/pinta-3.1.2-rpi5/patches/pinta-3.1.2-gtk48-backport.patch
  dotnet publish Pinta/Pinta.csproj -c Release -r linux-arm64 \
      --self-contained true -p:PublishSingleFile=false -o publish
  /path/to/pinta-3.1.2-rpi5/build-deb.sh publish

The resulting package is arm64-only and targets Raspberry Pi OS
Bookworm / Debian 12 with GTK 4.8 and libadwaita 1.2.

 -- Pinta RPi5 Backport <pinta-rpi5@users.noreply.github.com>
